---A Service resource is a logical component of an application that can share state and communicate in a secure fashion with other services. For example, an application that handles customer requests might include separate services to handle tasks such as backend data analysis or API requests from mobile devices. Each service has a collection of versions that define a specific set of code used to implement the functionality of that service.
---@class gcp.unstable.appengine_v1beta.Service
---@field id? string Output only. Relative name of the service within the application. Example: default.@OutputOnly
---@field name? string Output only. Full path to the Service resource in the API. Example: apps/myapp/services/default.@OutputOnly
---@field generatedCustomerMetadata? gcp.unstable.appengine_v1beta.DocumentMap Additional Google Generated Customer Metadata, this field won't be provided by default and can be requested by setting the IncludeExtraData field in GetServiceRequest
---@field split? gcp.unstable.appengine_v1beta.TrafficSplit Mapping that defines fractional HTTP traffic diversion to different versions within the service.
---@field networkSettings? gcp.unstable.appengine_v1beta.NetworkSettings Ingress settings for this service. Will apply to all versions.
---@field labels? gcp.unstable.appengine_v1beta.StringMap A set of labels to apply to this service. Labels are key/value pairs that describe the service and all resources that belong to it (e.g., versions). The labels can be used to search and group resources, and are propagated to the usage and billing reports, enabling fine-grain analysis of costs. An example of using labels is to tag resources belonging to different environments (e.g., "env=prod", "env=qa"). Label keys and values can be no longer than 63 characters and can only contain lowercase letters, numeric characters, underscores, dashes, and international characters. Label keys must start with a lowercase letter or an international character. Each service can have at most 32 labels.

---@alias gcp.unstable.appengine_v1beta.ServiceList gcp.unstable.appengine_v1beta.Service[]

---SSL configuration for a DomainMapping resource.
---@class gcp.unstable.appengine_v1beta.SslSettings
---@field sslManagementType? gcp.unstable.appengine_v1beta.SslSettingsSslManagementTypeEnum|string SSL management type for this domain. If AUTOMATIC, a managed certificate is automatically provisioned. If MANUAL, certificate_id must be manually specified in order to configure SSL for this domain.
---@field pendingManagedCertificateId? string Output only. ID of the managed AuthorizedCertificate resource currently being provisioned, if applicable. Until the new managed certificate has been successfully provisioned, the previous SSL state will be preserved. Once the provisioning process completes, the certificate_id field will reflect the new managed certificate and this field will be left empty. To remove SSL support while there is still a pending managed certificate, clear the certificate_id field with an UpdateDomainMappingRequest.@OutputOnly
---@field certificateId? string ID of the AuthorizedCertificate resource configuring SSL for the application. Clearing this field will remove SSL support.By default, a managed certificate is automatically created for every domain mapping. To omit SSL support or to configure SSL manually, specify SslManagementType.MANUAL on a CREATE or UPDATE request. You must be authorized to administer the AuthorizedCertificate resource to manually map it to a DomainMapping resource. Example: 12345.

---@alias gcp.unstable.appengine_v1beta.SslSettingsSslManagementTypeEnum "AUTOMATIC"|"MANUAL"

---Scheduler settings for standard environment.
---@class gcp.unstable.appengine_v1beta.StandardSchedulerSettings
---@field targetCpuUtilization? number Target CPU utilization ratio to maintain when scaling.
---@field minInstances? number Minimum number of instances to run for this version. Set to zero to disable min_instances configuration.
---@field maxInstances? number Maximum number of instances to run for this version. Set to 2147483647 to disable max_instances configuration.
---@field targetThroughputUtilization? number Target throughput utilization ratio to maintain when scaling

---Files served directly to the user for a given URL, such as images, CSS stylesheets, or JavaScript source files. Static file handlers describe which files in the application directory are static files, and which URLs serve them.
---@class gcp.unstable.appengine_v1beta.StaticFilesHandler
---@field requireMatchingFile? boolean Whether this handler should match the request if the file referenced by the handler does not exist.
---@field httpHeaders? gcp.unstable.appengine_v1beta.StringMap HTTP headers to use for all responses from these URLs.
---@field expiration? string Time a static file served by this handler should be cached by web proxies and browsers.
---@field path? string Path to the static files matched by the URL pattern, from the application root directory. The path can refer to text matched in groupings in the URL pattern.
---@field mimeType? string MIME type used to serve all files served by this handler.Defaults to file-specific MIME types, which are derived from each file's filename extension.
---@field applicationReadable? boolean Whether files should also be uploaded as code data. By default, files declared in static file handlers are uploaded as static data and are only served to end users; they cannot be read by the application. If enabled, uploads are charged against both your code and static data storage resource quotas.
---@field uploadPathRegex? string Regular expression that matches the file paths for all files that should be referenced by this handler.

---The Status type defines a logical error model that is suitable for different programming environments, including REST APIs and RPC APIs. It is used by gRPC (https://github.com/grpc). Each Status message contains three pieces of data: error code, error message, and error details.You can find out more about this error model and how to work with it in the API Design Guide (https://cloud.google.com/apis/design/errors).
---@class gcp.unstable.appengine_v1beta.Status
---@field code? number The status code, which should be an enum value of google.rpc.Code.
---@field message? string A developer-facing error message, which should be in English. Any user-facing error message should be localized and sent in the google.rpc.Status.details field, or localized by the client.
---@field details? gcp.unstable.appengine_v1beta.DocumentMapList A list of messages that carry the error details. There is a common set of message types for APIs to use.

---@alias gcp.unstable.appengine_v1beta.StringList string[]

---@alias gcp.unstable.appengine_v1beta.StringMap { [string]: string }

---Traffic routing configuration for versions within a single service. Traffic splits define how traffic directed to the service is assigned to versions.
---@class gcp.unstable.appengine_v1beta.TrafficSplit
---@field shardBy? gcp.unstable.appengine_v1beta.TrafficSplitShardByEnum|string Mechanism used to determine which version a request is sent to. The traffic selection algorithm will be stable for either type until allocations are changed.
---@field allocations? gcp.unstable.appengine_v1beta.DoubleMap Mapping from version IDs within the service to fractional (0.000, 1] allocations of traffic for that version. Each version can be specified only once, but some versions in the service may not have any traffic allocation. Services that have traffic allocated cannot be deleted until either the service is deleted or their traffic allocation is removed. Allocations must sum to 1. Up to two decimal place precision is supported for IP-based splits and up to three decimal places is supported for cookie-based splits.

---@alias gcp.unstable.appengine_v1beta.TrafficSplitShardByEnum "UNSPECIFIED"|"COOKIE"|"IP"|"RANDOM"

---Rules to match an HTTP request and dispatch that request to a service.
---@class gcp.unstable.appengine_v1beta.UrlDispatchRule
---@field path? string Pathname within the host. Must start with a "/". A single "*" can be included at the end of the path.The sum of the lengths of the domain and path may not exceed 100 characters.
---@field service? string Resource ID of a service in this application that should serve the matched request. The service must already exist. Example: default.
---@field domain? string Domain name to match against. The wildcard "*" is supported if specified before a period: "*.".Defaults to matching all domains: "*".

---@alias gcp.unstable.appengine_v1beta.UrlDispatchRuleList gcp.unstable.appengine_v1beta.UrlDispatchRule[]

---URL pattern and description of how the URL should be handled. App Engine can handle URLs by executing application code or by serving static files uploaded with the version, such as images, CSS, or JavaScript.
---@class gcp.unstable.appengine_v1beta.UrlMap
---@field script? gcp.unstable.appengine_v1beta.ScriptHandler Executes a script to handle the requests that match this URL pattern. Only the auto value is supported for Node.js in the App Engine standard environment, for example "script": "auto".
---@field staticFiles? gcp.unstable.appengine_v1beta.StaticFilesHandler Returns the contents of a file, such as an image, as the response.
---@field redirectHttpResponseCode? gcp.unstable.appengine_v1beta.UrlMapRedirectHttpResponseCodeEnum|string 30x code to use when performing redirects for the secure field. Defaults to 302.
---@field urlRegex? string URL prefix. Uses regular expression syntax, which means regexp special characters must be escaped, but should not contain groupings. All URLs that begin with this prefix are handled by this handler, using the portion of the URL after the prefix as part of the file path.
---@field login? gcp.unstable.appengine_v1beta.UrlMapLoginEnum|string Level of login required to access this resource. Not supported for Node.js in the App Engine standard environment.
---@field authFailAction? gcp.unstable.appengine_v1beta.UrlMapAuthFailActionEnum|string Action to take when users access resources that require authentication. Defaults to redirect.
---@field apiEndpoint? gcp.unstable.appengine_v1beta.ApiEndpointHandler Uses API Endpoints to handle requests.
---@field securityLevel? gcp.unstable.appengine_v1beta.UrlMapSecurityLevelEnum|string Security (HTTPS) enforcement for this URL.

---@alias gcp.unstable.appengine_v1beta.UrlMapAuthFailActionEnum "AUTH_FAIL_ACTION_UNSPECIFIED"|"AUTH_FAIL_ACTION_REDIRECT"|"AUTH_FAIL_ACTION_UNAUTHORIZED"

---@alias gcp.unstable.appengine_v1beta.UrlMapList gcp.unstable.appengine_v1beta.UrlMap[]

---@alias gcp.unstable.appengine_v1beta.UrlMapLoginEnum "LOGIN_UNSPECIFIED"|"LOGIN_OPTIONAL"|"LOGIN_ADMIN"|"LOGIN_REQUIRED"

---@alias gcp.unstable.appengine_v1beta.UrlMapRedirectHttpResponseCodeEnum "REDIRECT_HTTP_RESPONSE_CODE_UNSPECIFIED"|"REDIRECT_HTTP_RESPONSE_CODE_301"|"REDIRECT_HTTP_RESPONSE_CODE_302"|"REDIRECT_HTTP_RESPONSE_CODE_303"|"REDIRECT_HTTP_RESPONSE_CODE_307"

---@alias gcp.unstable.appengine_v1beta.UrlMapSecurityLevelEnum "SECURE_UNSPECIFIED"|"SECURE_DEFAULT"|"SECURE_NEVER"|"SECURE_OPTIONAL"|"SECURE_ALWAYS"

---A Version resource is a specific set of source code and configuration files that are deployed into a service.
---@class gcp.unstable.appengine_v1beta.Version
---@field errorHandlers? gcp.unstable.appengine_v1beta.ErrorHandlerList Custom static error pages. Limited to 10KB per page.Only returned in GET requests if view=FULL is set.
---@field deployment? gcp.unstable.appengine_v1beta.Deployment Code and application artifacts that make up this version.Only returned in GET requests if view=FULL is set.
---@field env? string App Engine execution environment for this version.Defaults to standard.
---@field threadsafe? boolean Whether multiple requests can be dispatched to this version at once.
---@field apiConfig? gcp.unstable.appengine_v1beta.ApiConfigHandler Serving configuration for Google Cloud Endpoints (https://cloud.google.com/endpoints).Only returned in GET requests if view=FULL is set.
---@field diskUsageBytes? string Output only. Total size in bytes of all the files that are included in this version and currently hosted on the App Engine disk.@OutputOnly
---@field envVariables? gcp.unstable.appengine_v1beta.StringMap Environment variables available to the application.Only returned in GET requests if view=FULL is set.
---@field servingStatus? gcp.unstable.appengine_v1beta.VersionServingStatusEnum Current serving status of this version. Only the versions with a SERVING status create instances and can be billed.SERVING_STATUS_UNSPECIFIED is an invalid value. Defaults to SERVING.
---@field defaultExpiration? string Duration that static files should be cached by web proxies and browsers. Only applicable if the corresponding StaticFilesHandler (https://cloud.google.com/appengine/docs/admin-api/reference/rest/v1beta/apps.services.versions#StaticFilesHandler) does not specify its own expiration time.Only returned in GET requests if view=FULL is set.
---@field endpointsApiService? gcp.unstable.appengine_v1beta.EndpointsApiService Cloud Endpoints configuration.If endpoints_api_service is set, the Cloud Endpoints Extensible Service Proxy will be provided to serve the API implemented by the app.
---@field handlers? gcp.unstable.appengine_v1beta.UrlMapList An ordered list of URL-matching patterns that should be applied to incoming requests. The first matching URL handles the request and other request handlers are not attempted.Only returned in GET requests if view=FULL is set.
---@field createdBy? string Output only. Email address of the user who created this version.@OutputOnly
---@field runtime? string Desired runtime. Example: python27.
---@field runtimeMainExecutablePath? string The path or name of the app's main executable.
---@field readinessCheck? gcp.unstable.appengine_v1beta.ReadinessCheck Configures readiness health checking for instances. Unhealthy instances are not put into the backend traffic rotation.
---@field appEngineBundledServices? gcp.unstable.appengine_v1beta.VersionAppEngineBundledServicesItemEnumList List of specific App Engine Bundled Services that are enabled for this Version.
---@field nobuildFilesRegex? string Files that match this pattern will not be built into this version. Only applicable for Go runtimes.Only returned in GET requests if view=FULL is set.
---@field healthCheck? gcp.unstable.appengine_v1beta.HealthCheck Configures health checking for instances. Unhealthy instances are stopped and replaced with new instances. Only applicable in the App Engine flexible environment.
---@field runtimeApiVersion? string The version of the API in the given runtime environment. Please see the app.yaml reference for valid values at https://cloud.google.com/appengine/docs/standard//config/appref
---@field serviceAccount? string The identity that the deployed version will run as. Admin API will use the App Engine Appspot service account as default if this field is neither provided in app.yaml file nor through CLI flag.
---@field instanceClass? string Instance class that is used to run this version. Valid values are: AutomaticScaling: F1, F2, F4, F4_1G ManualScaling or BasicScaling: B1, B2, B4, B8, B4_1GDefaults to F1 for AutomaticScaling and B1 for ManualScaling or BasicScaling.
---@field versionUrl? string Output only. Serving URL for this version. Example: "https://myversion-dot-myservice-dot-myapp.appspot.com"@OutputOnly
---@field generatedCustomerMetadata? gcp.unstable.appengine_v1beta.DocumentMap Additional Google Generated Customer Metadata, this field won't be provided by default and can be requested by setting the IncludeExtraData field in GetVersionRequest
---@field vpcAccess? gcp.unstable.appengine_v1beta.VpcAccess Enables VPC access connectivity for standard apps.
---@field id? string Relative name of the version within the service. Example: v1. Version names can contain only lowercase letters, numbers, or hyphens. Reserved names: "default", "latest", and any name with the prefix "ah-".
---@field resources? gcp.unstable.appengine_v1beta.Resources Machine resources for this version. Only applicable in the App Engine flexible environment.
---@field appEngineApis? boolean Allows App Engine second generation runtimes to access the legacy bundled services.
---@field livenessCheck? gcp.unstable.appengine_v1beta.LivenessCheck Configures liveness health checking for instances. Unhealthy instances are stopped and replaced with new instances
---@field buildEnvVariables? gcp.unstable.appengine_v1beta.StringMap Environment variables available to the build environment.Only returned in GET requests if view=FULL is set.
---@field name? string Output only. Full path to the Version resource in the API. Example: apps/myapp/services/default/versions/v1.@OutputOnly
---@field automaticScaling? gcp.unstable.appengine_v1beta.AutomaticScaling Automatic scaling is based on request rate, response latencies, and other application metrics. Instances are dynamically created and destroyed as needed in order to handle traffic.
---@field vm? boolean Whether to deploy this version in a container on a virtual machine.
---@field createTime? string Time that this version was created.@OutputOnly
---@field network? gcp.unstable.appengine_v1beta.Network Extra network settings. Only applicable in the App Engine flexible environment.
---@field entrypoint? gcp.unstable.appengine_v1beta.Entrypoint The entrypoint for the application.
---@field runtimeChannel? string The channel of the runtime to use. Only available for some runtimes. Defaults to the default channel.
---@field flexibleRuntimeSettings? gcp.unstable.appengine_v1beta.FlexibleRuntimeSettings Settings for App Engine flexible runtimes.
---@field zones? gcp.unstable.appengine_v1beta.StringList The Google Compute Engine zones that are supported by this version in the App Engine flexible environment. Deprecated.
---@field manualScaling? gcp.unstable.appengine_v1beta.ManualScaling A service with manual scaling runs continuously, allowing you to perform complex initialization and rely on the state of its memory over time. Manually scaled versions are sometimes referred to as "backends".
---@field basicScaling? gcp.unstable.appengine_v1beta.BasicScaling A service with basic scaling will create an instance when the application receives a request. The instance will be turned down when the app becomes idle. Basic scaling is ideal for work that is intermittent or driven by user activity.
---@field libraries? gcp.unstable.appengine_v1beta.LibraryList Configuration for third-party Python runtime libraries that are required by the application.Only returned in GET requests if view=FULL is set.
---@field betaSettings? gcp.unstable.appengine_v1beta.StringMap Metadata settings that are supplied to this version to enable beta runtime features.
---@field vpcAccessConnector? gcp.unstable.appengine_v1beta.VpcAccessConnector Enables VPC connectivity for standard apps.
---@field inboundServices? gcp.unstable.appengine_v1beta.VersionInboundServicesItemEnumList Before an application can receive email or XMPP messages, the application must be configured to enable the service.

---@alias gcp.unstable.appengine_v1beta.VersionAppEngineBundledServicesItemEnum "BUNDLED_SERVICE_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"BUNDLED_SERVICE_TYPE_APP_IDENTITY_SERVICE"|"BUNDLED_SERVICE_TYPE_BLOBSTORE"|"BUNDLED_SERVICE_TYPE_CAPABILITY_SERVICE"|"BUNDLED_SERVICE_TYPE_DATASTORE_V3"|"BUNDLED_SERVICE_TYPE_DEFERRED"|"BUNDLED_SERVICE_TYPE_IMAGES"|"BUNDLED_SERVICE_TYPE_MAIL"|"BUNDLED_SERVICE_TYPE_MEMCACHE"|"BUNDLED_SERVICE_TYPE_MODULES"|"BUNDLED_SERVICE_TYPE_NAMESPACES"|"BUNDLED_SERVICE_TYPE_NDB"|"BUNDLED_SERVICE_TYPE_SEARCH"|"BUNDLED_SERVICE_TYPE_TASKQUEUES"|"BUNDLED_SERVICE_TYPE_URLFETCH"|"BUNDLED_SERVICE_TYPE_USERS"

---@alias gcp.unstable.appengine_v1beta.VersionAppEngineBundledServicesItemEnumList (gcp.unstable.appengine_v1beta.VersionAppEngineBundledServicesItemEnum|string)[]

---@alias gcp.unstable.appengine_v1beta.VersionInboundServicesItemEnum "INBOUND_SERVICE_UNSPECIFIED"|"INBOUND_SERVICE_MAIL"|"INBOUND_SERVICE_MAIL_BOUNCE"|"INBOUND_SERVICE_XMPP_ERROR"|"INBOUND_SERVICE_XMPP_MESSAGE"|"INBOUND_SERVICE_XMPP_SUBSCRIBE"|"INBOUND_SERVICE_XMPP_PRESENCE"|"INBOUND_SERVICE_CHANNEL_PRESENCE"|"INBOUND_SERVICE_WARMUP"

